        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ignore peak horsepower entirely. Compare <strong class="text-white">CFM for bulk debris</strong>, <strong class="text-white">water lift for restricted or wet work</strong>, and <strong class="text-white">air watts</strong> where a manufacturer is confident enough to publish it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then remember that the biggest performance variable is not on any spec sheet: <strong class="text-white">a loaded filter can halve airflow</strong>. Fit a bag, clean the cartridge between sessions, and check the hose cuffs for leaks — that will move real-world performance further than any two machines in the same price bracket differ.
          </p>
